---
title: Life-Affirming Warm Nacho Dip
description: Nacho dip with no cheese, just cashews and carrots blended smooth and baked under crushed corn chips.
tags: [dip]
course: side
icons: [carrot, pepper-hot, pan-food]
cuisine: Tex-Mex
difficulty: easy
author: Angela Liddon
source: The Oh She Glows Cookbook
adapted: true
servings: 8
---

= Sauce

Place the @raw cashews{1%cup} in a #medium bowl{} and add water to cover. Soak for at least ~soak{2%hours}, preferably overnight.

Drain and rinse the cashews.

Heat the oven to 400°F (205°C). Lightly grease a 2-quart #cast iron skillet{}(or casserole dish).

Place the @carrots{1%cup}(peeled and chopped) in a #small saucepan{} and add water to cover. Bring the water to a boil and cook the carrots for ~boil{5%minutes}, or until tender, then drain. The carrots can be steamed instead.

In a #blender{}(or food processor), combine the soaked cashews, cooked carrots, @nutritional yeast{4-6%tbsp}, @fresh lemon juice{2%tbsp}, @garlic clove{1}, @sea salt{1 1/4%tsp}, @chili powder{1%tbsp}, @onion powder{1%tbsp}, @cayenne pepper{1/4%tsp}, and @water{2/3%cup}. Blend until silky smooth. If the sauce is too thick, add more water a little at a time. Pour the sauce into a #large bowl{}.

= Dip

Stir the @chunky marinara sauce{1%cup}, @black olives{1%can}(drained), @./pickled-jalapenos{2%tbsp}(chopped), and @baby spinach{2-3%handfuls}(chopped) into the sauce until fully combined.

> **What's Changed** — Black olives and pickled jalapeños replace the book's sweet onion, and the chili and onion powders are turned up.

Pour the dip into the greased #&cast iron skillet{} and smooth it out. Sprinkle with the @corn chips{1/3%cup}(crushed).

> **Swaps** — Bread crumbs work in place of the corn chips.

Bake uncovered for ~bake{25-30%minutes}. Do not let the corn chips burn.

Garnish with the @scallions{1-2}(sliced) and, if you like, more jalapeños, @?red onions{}(diced), and @?avocados{}(diced).

Serve warm with @?tortilla chips{}, @?pita chips{}, or any vegetables you like.

> **Serving** — A cast iron skillet keeps the dip warm for about an hour.

> **Storing** — Keeps in an airtight container in the refrigerator for 3 to 5 days. Reheat leftovers in a 400°F (205°C) oven for 10 to 20 minutes.
